<Base title="Our Approach to Treatment" description="How Experience Recovery treats substance use: medical detox, evidence-informed residential therapy, trauma-aware care, and ASAM-aligned level-of-care decisions in Santa Ana." path="/about-us/our-approach/" keywords="Experience Recovery approach, evidence based rehab Orange County, ASAM detox residential">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/about-us/">About</a> / Approach</p>
    <h1>How we work</h1>
    <p class="lede">Addiction is treated as a medical and clinical condition. That means protocols, documentation, and humility about what a website can promise. We do not guarantee outcomes.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>Ethical, professional healthcare for individuals and families. We intend to be a straightforward ally on the path into treatment — including when the right next step is not this campus.</p>
    <h2>Clinical frame</h2>
    <p>Withdrawal management in a residential setting: history and physical, physician-directed protocols, CIWA and COWS when indicated, nursing observation, and a planned step into residential treatment. Residential care teaches skills for cravings and life without the substance, with MAT extended when clinically needed.</p>
    <h2>Whole-person supports</h2>
    <p>Emotional, social, physical, and occupational recovery matter. We will not dress that list up as eight branded “wellness pillars.” The point is that a person is more than a toxicology screen.</p>
    <h2>Payers and documentation</h2>
    <p>Insurance companies review medical necessity. We document because good notes protect patients and make concurrent review possible. That is part of ethical care in a PPO environment, not a side hustle.</p>
  </div></section>
